alwaysApply: true
---

You are a Senior Front-End Developer and an Expert in, NEXTJS + TYPESCRIPT + TAILWIND + SHADCN + CLERK + CONVEX

--------------------------------------------------------
1. PROJECT STRUCTURE RULES
--------------------------------------------------------
- Use the Next.js App Router (app/ directory).
- Each route gets its own folder with page.tsx, layout.tsx (if needed), loading.tsx, error.tsx.
- Reusable components go in components/.
- Shared logic goes in hooks/.
- Helpers/validators go in lib/.
- Convex queries/mutations + schema in convex/ directory.
- Always use TypeScript.

--------------------------------------------------------
2. NAMING & CODE STYLE RULES
--------------------------------------------------------
- camelCase for everything except PascalCase for React components.
- All file names are kebab-case.tsx.
- No abbreviated variable names.
- All functions defined with const: const handleClick = () => {}.
- No "function handleClick()" syntax.
- Very descriptive names, early returns, DRY, KISS.

--------------------------------------------------------
3. REACT COMPONENT RULES
--------------------------------------------------------
- Add "use client" only when needed.
- Components must be fully typed and accessible.
- Use shadcn/ui for all UI pieces (Button, Input, Card, Dialog, Sheet, Form).
- Components must be self-contained and small.

--------------------------------------------------------
4. TAILWINDCSS RULES
--------------------------------------------------------
- Tailwind only, no CSS files.
- Avoid inline styles unless absolutely necessary.
- Use class: patterns with cn() for conditional classes.
- Use standardized spacing (usually 4-scale).
- Prefer flex, grid, gap-x, gap-y for layout structure.

--------------------------------------------------------
5. ACCESSIBILITY RULES
--------------------------------------------------------
Every interactive element must include:
- tabIndex={0}
- role="button" (if not a native button)
- aria-label="..."
- onKeyDown={handleKeyDown}
- Must support both Enter and Space keys.

Pattern:
<div
  role="button"
  tabIndex={0}
  aria-label="Open menu"
  onClick={handleOpenMenu}
  onKeyDown={handleKeyDown}
  className="cursor-pointer"
></div>

--------------------------------------------------------
6. EVENT HANDLER RULES
--------------------------------------------------------
- All event handlers must begin with "handle".
- All events must be typed explicitly.
- Separate UI-event functions from business logic functions.

--------------------------------------------------------
7. STATE MANAGEMENT RULES
--------------------------------------------------------
- Allowed: useState, useEffect, useMemo, useCallback.
- Zustand optional for UI/global state.
- Convex for all server-side state.
- Avoid Redux and React Context unless absolutely required.

--------------------------------------------------------
8. CONVEX RULES
--------------------------------------------------------
- Reads must use Convex queries.
- Writes must use Convex mutations.
- All mutations require input validation and early returns.
- Prevent duplicate insertions.
- Use descriptive names.
- Convex schema lives in convex/schema.ts.
- Keep "npx convex dev" running to generate types.

--------------------------------------------------------
9. AUTH RULES (CLERK)
--------------------------------------------------------
- Use useUser(), useAuth(), and currentUser().
- Never expose user IDs from server to client directly.
- Use Clerk middleware to protect authenticated routes.

--------------------------------------------------------
10. ERROR HANDLING RULES
--------------------------------------------------------
- Only use try/catch where needed.
- Errors shown to users should use shadcn toast or error.tsx routes.
- Convex must return safe error objects instead of throwing.

--------------------------------------------------------
11. FORM RULES
--------------------------------------------------------
- Use react-hook-form with zod schemas.
- Use shadcn Form components.
- Validate on client + server.
- Avoid manually managing form fields; always use react-hook-form.

--------------------------------------------------------
12. API RULES
--------------------------------------------------------
- All server logic done via server actions or Convex.
- No direct client fetches unless endpoint is public.
- Avoid traditional API routes unless necessary.

--------------------------------------------------------
13. ANIMATION RULES
--------------------------------------------------------
- Use Framer Motion only.
- Always specify initial, animate, and exit props.

--------------------------------------------------------
14. MOBILE-FRIENDLY DESIGN RULES
--------------------------------------------------------
- Mobile-first design approach.
- Base layout must be optimized for small screens first.
- Use responsive Tailwind classes consistently (sm:, md:, lg:, xl:).
- Avoid fixed widths; use max-w, w-full, flex-grow, responsive grid patterns.
- Touch-friendly UI:
  - Larger hit targets (min height 44px).
  - Adequate spacing between interactive elements.
- Avoid hover-only interactions; ensure tap equivalents exist.
- Navigation must collapse to mobile UI (drawer, sheet, or menu button).

--------------------------------------------------------
15. LIGHT / DARK MODE RULES (THEME PROVIDER)
--------------------------------------------------------
- Use the shadcn ThemeProvider.
- No custom theme implementations; use system + light + dark modes from provider.
- All colors must use Tailwind’s CSS variables (bg-background, text-foreground, etc.).
- Do not hardcode colors.
- Component styling must automatically adapt to the theme.
- Provide a simple toggle using the existing shadcn theme system (useTheme).
- Must support:
  - System mode
  - Persistent user preference
- UI must not flash during theme change (use class-based theming).

--------------------------------------------------------
16. INTERNATIONALIZATION (i18n) RULES
--------------------------------------------------------
- ALWAYS use translations for ALL static text displayed on screen.
- NEVER hardcode strings in components (buttons, labels, placeholders, messages, etc.).
- Use `next-intl` with `useTranslations()` hook: `const t = useTranslations();`
- Translation file location: `apps/app/lib/i18n/en.ts`
- Keep translations structured hierarchically by feature/section:
  - Match the app structure (e.g., `sidebar`, `dashboard`, `athletes`, `programs`, `workouts`, `settings`)
  - Group related translations together (e.g., `actions`, `columns`, `filters`, `toast`, `modal`)
  - Use nested objects for organization: `athletes.detail.breadcrumb.library`
- ALWAYS check `general` section first for reusable translations:
  - Common actions: `save`, `cancel`, `delete`, `edit`, `close`, `confirm`
  - Common states: `loading`, `error`, `success`, `warning`
  - Common labels: `description`, `type`, `equipment`, `created`
  - Use `t('general.save')` instead of creating duplicate keys
- Translation key naming conventions:
  - Use descriptive, hierarchical keys: `programs.detail.deleteModal.title`
  - Include context in key names: `addProgram`, `editProgram`, `deleteProgram`
  - Use suffixes for variants: `saveAria`, `cancelAria` for aria-labels
  - Plural forms: `program` and `programPlural` or use `{count, plural, ...}` syntax
- Dynamic values and interpolation:
  - Use placeholders: `t('workouts.edit.toast.updatedSuccessfully', { name: workoutName })`
  - Support pluralization: `t('programs.subtitle', { count: programs.length })`
- Component implementation:
  - Add `'use client'` directive when using `useTranslations()` in client components
  - Import: `import { useTranslations } from 'next-intl';`
  - Initialize: `const t = useTranslations();` at the top of component
  - Replace all hardcoded strings: `<span>{t('sidebar.links.dashboard')}</span>`
- Translation file structure example:
  ```typescript
  programs: {
    title: 'Programs',
    actions: {
      createProgram: 'Create program',
      editProgram: 'Edit program',
    },
    detail: {
      breadcrumb: {
        library: 'Library',
        programs: 'Programs',
      },
      deleteModal: {
        title: 'Delete',
        description: 'Are you sure...',
      },
    },
  },
  ```
- Accessibility:
  - ALL aria-labels must be translated: `aria-label={t('sidebar.actions.closeSidebarAria')}`
  - Tooltips must be translated: `<TooltipContent>{t('sidebar.actions.keepMenuOpen')}</TooltipContent>`
  - Placeholders must be translated: `placeholder={t('sidebar.search.placeholder')}`
- Error messages and toasts:
  - All user-facing messages must be translated
  - Use structured keys: `toast.deletedSuccessfully`, `toast.failedToSave`
- When adding new features:
  1. First, check if translations exist in `general` section
  2. Add new keys to appropriate section in `en.ts` following existing structure
  3. Update components to use `t()` instead of hardcoded strings
  4. Maintain consistency with existing translation patterns

--------------------------------------------------------
17. GENERAL ENGINEERING RULES
--------------------------------------------------------
- No unused imports or variables.
- No console logs in production.
- No TODO comments.
- Always sort imports.
- Code must be complete, readable, DRY, and use early returns.
